==== Part 0 - Prerequisites ====
  - Plug in a USB flash drive into your computer and format it to FAT32 file system. Only ~12MB of space is needed.
  - Keep this guide open on your computer. You will temporarily lose internet access when you plug in your new router.
  - Download the latest version of these three images for DL-WRX36 via [[https://firmware-selector.openwrt.org/|Firmware Selector]] prior to installation:
    * "initramfs" (aka kernel) image for initial access (mandatory)
    * "factory" image for flashing to OpenWrt (mandatory)
    * "sysupgrade" image for updating to latest version of OpenWrt (optional)
  - To use the pre-configured file that enables SSH (recommended), download it [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8072a-technical-discussion/110454/670|from the forum]].
  - The steps below adapted from the [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-install/153280/68|forum]] refer to 23.05, remember to use the latest image filenames at the time of your install.
  - Note the filename changes. For 23.05: ipq807x-generic. For Snapshots/24.10 onward: qualcommax-ipq807x.
  - OEM password for SSH/Web is: askey1234

It is recommended to **copy and paste commands** provided below to avoid typos which could result in needing a serial recovery.

==== Part 1 - Copy and boot initramfs ====

__**Complete 'Part 1 option A' OR 'Part 1 option B' to boot "initramfs", then use Part 2 to install the "factory" OpenWrt image.**__

<tabbox Part 1, option A - Use SSH on the OEM firmware to copy and boot "initramfs">
  - Copy the initramfs image to the FAT32-formatted flash drive from Part 0.
  - Disconnect the USB flash drive from your computer and plug it into the USB port on the back of the router.
  - Plug an ethernet cable into your computer and the other end into your router on one of the four LAN ports (labeled ETH1-ETH4) and NOT the WAN port (labeled INTERNET).
  - Plug the power cord into the back of the router and then plug it into a power outlet.
  - Open a browser and go to http://login.dynalink.
  - Enter the credentials found on the bottom of the router.
  - Enable SSH on the router (choose either bullet point **a** OR bullet point **b**):
    - Upload the pre-configured router config file that you downloaded in Part 0.
      - Go to "System Settings" > "Configuration and Reset" tab.
      - Click "Select file", choose `backup.cfg`, then click "Upload".
      - Wait for the router to reboot.
      - Log into the router over SSH: <code>ssh -o HostKeyAlgorithms=+ssh-rsa -o PubkeyAcceptedKeyTypes=+ssh-rsa admin@192.168.216.1</code>
    - Manually enable SSH access as described in [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8072a-openwrt-support/110454/365|this forum post]].
  - Change the boot command so it loads the initramfs image on next boot (fallback to OEM firmware is provided):
    - In this example we use 23.05.5 stable, run:<code># fw_setenv bootcmd 'usb start && fatload usb 0:1 0x44000000 openwrt-23.05.5-ipq807x-generic-dynalink_dl-wrx36-initramfs-uImage.itb && bootm 0x44000000; bootipq'</code>
    - If you are installing a snapshot, run:<code># fw_setenv bootcmd 'usb start && fatload usb 0:1 0x44000000 openwrt-qualcommax-ipq807x-dynalink_dl-wrx36-initramfs-uImage.itb && bootm 0x44000000; bootipq'</code>
  - Reboot the device to boot the initramfs:<code># reboot</code>
  - Continue to Part 2 of the installation guide.

<tabbox Part 1, option B - Use a serial connection (3.3V) to copy and boot "initramfs">
If you're planning on using serial for flashing but the serial output stops at "S - Core 0 Frequency, 1651 MHz", read [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8072a-technical-discussion/110454/1146|this forum post]] for instructions on how to fix it.

  - Stop auto boot to get to U-boot shell.
  - Transfer initramfs image to device using TFTP and a FAT32-formatted USB flash drive. Adjust filenames for qualcommax if needed.
    - For USB run:<code># usb start
# fatload usb 0:1 0x44000000 openwrt-ipq807x-generic-dynalink_dl-wrx36-initramfs-uImage.itb</code>
    - For TFTP run:<code># setenv serverip 192.168.1.10 (IP of TFTP server host)
# setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1 (IP used by the router, for getting the image, must be in the same subnet as the TFTP host)
# tftpboot openwrt-ipq807x-generic-dynalink_dl-wrx36-initramfs-fit-uImage.itb</code>
  - Boot the initramfs image:<code># bootm</code>
  - Continue to Part 2 of the installation guide.
</tabbox>

==== Part 2 - Copy and boot the OpenWrt factory image====
  * The default LAN IP of the booted initramfs is 192.168.1.1. If you're unable to connect to 192.168.1.1, the initramfs boot failed, and the router is still running the Dynalink firmware.
  * WinSCP & scp now default to the SFTP protocol, make sure to tell your application to use the scp protocol.

  - Copy the OpenWrt factory image to the router and store it in /tmp<code>$ scp openwrt-23.05.5-ipq807x-generic-dynalink_dl-wrx36-squashfs-factory.ubi root@192.168.1.1:/tmp/factory_image.ubi</code>
  - Connect to the device over SSH (on a LAN port)<code>$ ssh root@192.168.1.1</code>
  - Check the MTD partition table. rootfs and rootfs_1 should be mtd18 and mtd20 depending on the current OEM slot.<code># cat /proc/mtd</code>
  - Format both rootfs partitions:<code># ubiformat /dev/mtd18 -y -f /tmp/factory_image.ubi
# ubiformat /dev/mtd20 -y -f /tmp/factory_image.ubi</code>
  - Set the mapping for the U-Boot device id:<code># fw_setenv mtdids 'nand0=nand0'</code>
  - Get the offset of mtd18 to determine the current OEM slot:<code># cat /sys/class/mtd/mtd18/offset</code>
    - If the current offset is 16777216  (0x1000000), the current OEM slot is 1.
    - If the current offset is 127926272 (0x7a00000), the current OEM slot is 2.
  - Define the flash partitions:
    - If the current OEM slot is 1, run:<code># fw_setenv mtdparts 'mtdparts=nand0:0x6100000@0x1000000(fs),0x6100000@0x7a00000(fs_1)'</code>
    - If the current OEM slot is 2, run:<code># fw_setenv mtdparts 'mtdparts=nand0:0x6100000@0x7a00000(fs),0x6100000@0x1000000(fs_1)'</code>
  - Set the boot command to use the firmware image flashed above: <code>
# fw_setenv bootcmd 'setenv bootargs console=ttyMSM0,115200n8 ubi.mtd=rootfs rootfstype=squashfs rootwait; ubi part fs; ubi read 0x44000000 kernel; bootm 0x44000000#config@rt5010w-d350-rev0'</code>
  - Check that the u-boot variables have set correctly. You can do that with <code># fw_printenv</code>
  - Unplug the USB from the back of the router.
  - Reboot the device:<code># reboot</code>
  - OPTIONAL (can be also done later): Set the boot command to use the USB as a fail-safe in case something goes wrong. That is done by setting three u-boot variables: defining the USB boot routine (actually same as in part 1), normal OpenWrt boot routine (same as normal single bootcmd), and then setting the bootcmd to try to use those two routines consecutively. Make sure that you set the filename in the command below below to match the actual image you placed on the USB stick (e.g. snapshots and 24.10 have qualcommax in the name, while this example uses the 23.05.5 name). More details about this fail-safe method can be found in [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8072a-technical-discussion/110454/1317|this forum comment]].<code>$ ssh root@192.168.1.1

# fw_setenv openwrtboot 'setenv bootargs console=ttyMSM0,115200n8 ubi.mtd=rootfs rootfstype=squashfs rootwait; ubi part fs; ubi read 0x44000000 kernel; bootm 0x44000000#config@rt5010w-d350-rev0'
# fw_setenv openwrtusb 'usb start && fatload usb 0:1 0x44000000 openwrt-23.05.5-ipq807x-generic-dynalink_dl-wrx36-initramfs-uImage.itb && bootm 0x44000000'
# fw_setenv bootcmd 'run openwrtusb; run openwrtboot'
</code>

Installation is complete. OpenWrt updates may now be flashed with LuCI using a "sysupgrade" image.

===== Return to stock =====

1. Capture an OTA image or download from the [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8074-openwrt-support/110454/124|forum post]] one to [[https://mega.nz/file/VIEiHCRZ#m8cCR544jPxXC2QLtA7KmmMW401kr7niTgYD_tZHZyU|mega.nz]]
<code>
# md5sum Dynalink-RT5010W-d350-V1.10.01.201_sysupgrade_firmware_wififw.bin
c368dbf24e24df16d61b97a40feb5a92  Dynalink-RT5010W-d350-V1.10.01.201_sysupgrade_firmware_wififw.bin
</code>

2. Ubiformat the extracted stock rootfs - as documented on this forum [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8072a-technical-discussion/110454/398
|post]], make sure you use a recent (>= 2022.Q4) u-boot dumpimage.

3. OEM default passwords: SSH/WebUI: askey1234, WiFi: check your bottom label.

