===== Community Builds =====

  - Custom NSS builds on the [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/qualcommax-nss-build/148529|forum]] adds hardware offloading support for ipq807x. Note these are unofficial and may be less stable.
  - jkool702 builds on the [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/full-featured-custom-build-for-dynalink-dl-wrx36-ax3600/180168|forum]] include kernel level performance tweaks for low latency.

===== Notes =====

  - The OEM firmware has dual-image support for fail safe. This feature is not supported by [[:packages:pkgdata:luci-app-advanced-reboot|advanced-reboot]] for this device.
  - With ifconfig it might appear this device uses DSA, however it actually uses a switchdev driver. [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/dynalink-dl-wrx36-askey-rt5010w-ipq8072a-technical-discussion/110454/2189|See explanation]].
  - This device is based on the Askey RT5010W. Internal hardware and OEM firmware are nearly identical. In fact the PCB says RT5010W (seen on "PCB Top - Heatsink Removed" photo above). There are some minor differences with the case color and the Askey has a power switch.

